-- title:
--   Same kernel, generation and equal degree force an isomorphism
-- statement:
--   Let $K$, $E$, $F$, $F'$ be fields and $R$ a commutative ring, all four of $E$, $R$, $F$, $F'$ being $K$-algebras, and let $j : E \to R$, $\alpha : R \to F$, $\beta : R \to F'$ be $K$-algebra homomorphisms. Assume: (i) the kernels of the underlying ring homomorphisms of $\alpha$ and $\beta$ coincide as ideals of $R$; (ii) the subfield of $F$ generated by the set-theoretic range of $\alpha$ is all of $F$; (iii) `FiniteAlong K (α.comp j)` and `FiniteAlong K (β.comp j)`, that is, $F$ is a finite module over $E$ for the $E$-algebra structure obtained by transporting scalars along $\alpha \circ j$, and likewise $F'$ is a finite $E$-module along $\beta \circ j$; (iv) `finrankAlong` of these two structures agree, i.e. the $E$-module ranks of $F$ (along $\alpha \circ j$) and of $F'$ (along $\beta \circ j$) are the same natural number. The conclusion is that there exists a $K$-algebra isomorphism $\iota : F \simeq F'$ such that $\alpha$ followed by $\iota$ equals $\beta$ as $K$-algebra homomorphisms $R \to F'$.
--
--   This is the purely field-theoretic uniqueness statement behind identifications of function fields: a field generated by the image of $\alpha$ is determined, together with the map from $R$, by the kernel, once the degrees over a common base field $E$ agree. It is used in the identification of the level fields of the quaternionic moduli tower, in [`CerednikDrinfeld.QM.ModuliTowerWitnessD.exists_algEquiv_level_comp_phi_eq_of_pt_pullback_of_two_mul_dvd`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.QM.ModuliTowerWitnessD.exists_algEquiv_level_comp_phi_eq_of_pt_pullback_of_two_mul_dvd).
